{% comment %}
HappyFox — renders a glanceable help-desk dashboard from the serverless aggregator
(serverless.js). That `run(input)` returns an ordered `cards` array of
{ key, label, value, scope, name } for the user-selected metrics, plus `updated`
(ISO-8601 UTC) and `error`. Because it's a single data source, those keys arrive as
top-level merge variables, so the four size files pass `cards`, `updated`, and `error`
straight through.

Layout model (v0.4): one user-chosen HERO (big number) sits up top, then the remaining
metrics split by scope into ME (`my_*`) and ALL (`all_*`). Full / half-horizontal render each
scope with the `scope_group` template (a ME/ALL header over a grid of cards, capped in Liquid
with a "+N more" tail). Half-vertical is the tall one: it hands every card to the framework
overflow engine (the `overflow_scope` partial — two `.list` columns) so it fills the real
height and overflows itself. `card.scope` ('my'/'all') drives the split; `card.name` is the
scope-stripped label ("Open" instead of "My Open") so the header carries the scope. The hero
is whichever metric matches the `hero` custom field, falling back to the first card. All
rendering lives here; the four size files are thin {% raw %}{% render 'main', ... %}{% endraw %} wrappers that pass a `layout_size`.
{% endcomment %}

{% comment %} ---- one stat: a value over its (optionally scope-stripped) label ---- {% endcomment %}
{% template card %}
<div class="item">
  <div class="meta"></div>
  <div class="content">
    <span class="value {{ value_size | default: 'value--small' }} value--tnums"{% if card.value != nil %} data-value-format="true" data-fit-value="true"{% endif %}>{{ card.value | default: '—' }}</span>
    <span class="label {{ label_size | default: 'label--small' }}" data-clamp="2">{{ label_text | default: card.label }}</span>
  </div>
</div>
{% endtemplate %}

{% comment %} ---- title bar: inline HappyFox mark, instance name, last-updated time ---- {% endcomment %}
{% template title_bar %}
<div class="title_bar">
  <svg class="image" viewBox="0 0 18.979 18.835" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg">
    <g transform="translate(0 -.56641)" clip-path="url(#hf_clip0)">
      <g clip-path="url(#hf_clip1)" fill="#ff5a00">
        <path d="m2.5832 8.0872c0.40387 0 0.80012-0.1143 1.143-0.33275l4.1276-2.6188-5.7964-4.2241c-0.856-0.62486-2.0574-0.0127-2.0574 1.044v4.435l1.077 1.0719c0.40387 0.40133 0.93728 0.62232 1.5088 0.62232z"/>
        <path d="m0.45213 12.27 5.931 5.0928 2.0117 1.7273c0.46991 0.4038 1.1583 0.4165 1.6434 0.033l8.4483-6.6626c0.3099-0.2464 0.4927-0.6198 0.4927-1.016v-9.5811c0-1.0389-1.1658-1.6561-2.0244-1.0694l-7.7776 5.3087-4.6356 2.9414c-0.60199 0.38355-1.2827 0.56897-1.9584 0.56897-0.94236 0-1.8771-0.36323-2.5832-1.0668v2.7432c0 0.3785 0.1651 0.7367 0.45213 0.9805z"/>
      </g>
    </g>
    <defs>
      <clipPath id="hf_clip0"><rect width="105.15" height="20" fill="#fff"/></clipPath>
      <clipPath id="hf_clip1"><rect transform="translate(0 .56641)" width="18.979" height="18.835" fill="#fff"/></clipPath>
    </defs>
  </svg>
  {% if layout_size == 'full' or layout_size == 'half-horizontal' %}
  <span class="title">{{ trmnl.plugin_settings.instance_name | default: 'HappyFox' }}</span>
  {% endif %}
  {% if updated_display %}
  <span class="instance">Updated {{ updated_display }}</span>
  {% endif %}
</div>
{% endtemplate %}

{% comment %}
---- one scope group (full / half-horizontal): a ME/ALL header over the scope's non-hero cards,
capped at `item_limit` with a hand-rendered "+N more" tail. `total_count` is the scope's
non-hero card count (precomputed in `main`). `inner_class` is the card container: a
`grid grid--cols-N` so the two scope rows align column-to-column. Everything in the scope chain
carries `self--stretch` — the per-size middle container, the scope_group root, and the inner
card grid — because each level is a `flex--col` (`align-items:center`), which otherwise shrinks
+ centers a short grid to its content width. The header `self--start` keeps it left. Capping is
explicit because the framework overflow engine wants to distribute into columns, not pack a
single horizontal row — half-vertical uses that engine instead (see `overflow_scope` below).
{% endcomment %}
{% template scope_group %}
<div class="flex flex--col gap--small self--stretch">
  <span class="label label--small self--start">{{ heading }}</span>
  <div class="{{ inner_class | default: 'flex flex--col gap--small' }} self--stretch">
    {% assign shown = 0 %}
    {% for card in scope_cards %}{% unless card.key == hero_key %}{% if shown < item_limit %}
    {% render 'card', card: card, label_text: card.name, value_size: value_size, label_size: label_size %}
    {% assign shown = shown | plus: 1 %}
    {% endif %}{% endunless %}{% endfor %}
    {% assign hidden = total_count | minus: shown %}
    {% if hidden > 0 %}
    <span class="label label--small self--center no-shrink">+{{ hidden }} more</span>
    {% endif %}
  </div>
</div>
{% endtemplate %}

{% comment %}
---- one half-vertical scope: a labeled `.list` column handed to the framework overflow engine
(`data-overflow` + `-max-height="auto"` + `-counter`), which shows as many cards as fit the real
portrait height and appends "and N more" itself. half-vertical is the one size that must FILL the
height, so it diverges from `scope_group`'s static cap. `stretch` on the row + each `.list` gives
the engine a bounded height to measure against so it caps instead of overrunning. ----
{% endcomment %}
{% template overflow_scope %}
<div class="list stretch" data-overflow="true" data-overflow-max-height="auto" data-overflow-counter="true" data-overflow-max-cols="1">
  <span class="label label--small">{{ heading }}</span>
  {% for card in scope_cards %}{% unless card.key == hero_key %}
  {% render 'card', card: card, label_text: card.name, value_size: 'value--small lg:value--base', label_size: 'label--small' %}
  {% endunless %}{% endfor %}
</div>
{% endtemplate %}

{% template main %}
{% comment %} time mask: respect the 12/24-hour custom field {% endcomment %}
{% if trmnl.plugin_settings.custom_fields_values.timemode == '24_hour' %}
{% assign mask_time = '%H:%M' %}
{% else %}
{% assign mask_time = '%-I:%M%P' %}
{% endif %}

{% comment %} aggregator stamps `updated` as ISO-8601 UTC; shift to the user's local time {% endcomment %}
{% assign updated_display = nil %}
{% if updated %}
{% assign updated_local = updated | date: '%s' | plus: trmnl.user.utc_offset | date: '%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%S%z' %}
{% assign updated_display = updated_local | l_date: mask_time, trmnl.user.locale %}
{% endif %}

{% if error != blank or cards == blank %}
{%- comment -%} Empty / error state {%- endcomment -%}
<div class="layout layout--center">
  <span class="label lg:label--large text--center" data-clamp="3">{{ error | default: 'No HappyFox Data' }}</span>
</div>

{% else %}
{% comment %} Resolve the hero: the card matching the `hero` field, else the first card. {% endcomment %}
{% assign hero = cards[0] %}
{% assign hero_pick = trmnl.plugin_settings.custom_fields_values.hero %}
{% if hero_pick %}
{% assign hero_match = cards | where: 'key', hero_pick %}
{% if hero_match.size > 0 %}{% assign hero = hero_match[0] %}{% endif %}
{% endif %}
{% assign hero_key = hero.key %}

{% comment %} Split the supporting cards by scope (hero excluded at render time). {% endcomment %}
{% assign my_cards = cards | where: 'scope', 'my' %}
{% assign all_cards = cards | where: 'scope', 'all' %}
{% assign my_extra = 0 %}{% if hero.scope == 'my' %}{% assign my_extra = 1 %}{% endif %}
{% assign all_extra = 0 %}{% if hero.scope == 'all' %}{% assign all_extra = 1 %}{% endif %}
{% assign my_count = my_cards.size | minus: my_extra %}
{% assign all_count = all_cards.size | minus: all_extra %}

{% case layout_size %}

{% comment %} ================= FULL (800x480) ================= {% endcomment %}
{% when 'full' %}
<div class="layout layout--col">
  <div class="grid">
    {% render 'card', card: hero, value_size: 'value--xxxlarge lg:value--giga', label_size: 'label--large' %}
  </div>
  {% if my_count > 0 or all_count > 0 %}
  <div class="divider"></div>
  <div class="flex flex--col gap--space-between grow self--stretch">
    {% if my_count > 0 %}
    {% render 'scope_group', heading: 'Me', scope_cards: my_cards, hero_key: hero_key, total_count: my_count, item_limit: 5, inner_class: 'grid grid--cols-6', value_size: 'value--large lg:value--xlarge', label_size: 'label--small lg:label--base' %}
    {% endif %}
    {% if my_count > 0 and all_count > 0 %}
    <div class="divider"></div>
    {% endif %}
    {% if all_count > 0 %}
    {% render 'scope_group', heading: 'All', scope_cards: all_cards, hero_key: hero_key, total_count: all_count, item_limit: 5, inner_class: 'grid grid--cols-6', value_size: 'value--large lg:value--xlarge', label_size: 'label--small lg:label--base' %}
    {% endif %}
  </div>
  {% endif %}
</div>

{% comment %} ============ HALF-HORIZONTAL (800x240) ============ {% endcomment %}
{% when 'half-horizontal' %}
<div class="layout">
  <div class="flex flex--row gap--large flex--center-y grow">
    <div class="no-shrink">
      {% render 'card', card: hero, value_size: 'value--xxlarge lg:value--xxxlarge', label_size: 'label--base lg:label--large' %}
    </div>
    {% if my_count > 0 or all_count > 0 %}
    <div class="flex flex--col gap--small grow">
      {% if my_count > 0 %}
      {% render 'scope_group', heading: 'Me', scope_cards: my_cards, hero_key: hero_key, total_count: my_count, item_limit: 4, inner_class: 'grid grid--cols-5', value_size: 'value--small', label_size: 'label--small' %}
      {% endif %}
      {% if all_count > 0 %}
      {% render 'scope_group', heading: 'All', scope_cards: all_cards, hero_key: hero_key, total_count: all_count, item_limit: 4, inner_class: 'grid grid--cols-5', value_size: 'value--small', label_size: 'label--small' %}
      {% endif %}
    </div>
    {% endif %}
  </div>
</div>

{% comment %} ============= HALF-VERTICAL (400x480, taller in portrait) ============= {% endcomment %}
{% comment %} Narrow + tall, and much taller in portrait — the one size that must FILL the height.
Its two `Me | All` columns use the `overflow_scope` partial (framework overflow engine); the
`stretch` on this row gives them a bounded height to measure against so the engine caps instead
of overrunning. {% endcomment %}
{% when 'half-vertical' %}
<div class="layout layout--col">
  <div class="grid">
    {% render 'card', card: hero, value_size: 'value--large lg:value--xlarge', label_size: 'label--base lg:label--large' %}
  </div>
  {% if my_count > 0 or all_count > 0 %}
  <div class="divider"></div>
  <div class="flex flex--row gap--small stretch">
    {% if my_count > 0 %}{% render 'overflow_scope', heading: 'Me', scope_cards: my_cards, hero_key: hero_key %}{% endif %}
    {% if all_count > 0 %}{% render 'overflow_scope', heading: 'All', scope_cards: all_cards, hero_key: hero_key %}{% endif %}
  </div>
  {% endif %}
</div>

{% comment %} ================ QUADRANT (400x240) ================ {% endcomment %}
{% comment %} too small for labeled scope columns: hero on the left + the next four metrics in a
2x2 grid (full labels carry the scope), filling the width instead of a short single column. {% endcomment %}
{% when 'quadrant' %}
<div class="layout">
  <div class="flex flex--row gap--small flex--center-y grow">
    <div class="no-shrink">
      {% render 'card', card: hero, value_size: 'value--xlarge lg:value--xxlarge', label_size: 'label--small lg:label--base' %}
    </div>
    {% if cards.size > 1 %}
    <div class="grid grid--cols-2 grow self--stretch">
      {% assign shown = 0 %}
      {% for card in cards %}{% unless card.key == hero_key %}{% if shown < 4 %}
      {% render 'card', card: card, value_size: 'value--small lg:value--base', label_size: 'label--small' %}
      {% assign shown = shown | plus: 1 %}
      {% endif %}{% endunless %}{% endfor %}
    </div>
    {% endif %}
  </div>
</div>

{% endcase %}
{% endif %}

{% render 'title_bar', trmnl: trmnl, layout_size: layout_size, updated_display: updated_display %}
{% endtemplate %}
